From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 18:20:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] AESinkALSA: another card than the AML one takes every format

On S5 and later, the AML card carries TrueHD and DTS-HD MA on surround71
and the other bitstreams on hdmi, and the formats each device is offered
are set accordingly. That split was applied to any card's surround71, so
binaural's loopback (Virtual Sound) was offered TrueHD and DTS-HD MA only:
an E-AC-3 film with Atmos objects was decoded by Kodi to its 5.1 core
instead of reaching binaural, which decodes the objects.

The split now applies to the AML card's devices; another card's device is
offered every format, as on older SoCs.

Signed-off-by: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 xbmc/cores/AudioEngine/Sinks/AESinkALSA.cpp | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/xbmc/cores/AudioEngine/Sinks/AESinkALSA.cpp b/xbmc/cores/AudioEngine/Sinks/AESinkALSA.cpp
--- a/xbmc/cores/AudioEngine/Sinks/AESinkALSA.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/cores/AudioEngine/Sinks/AESinkALSA.cpp
@@ -1930,7 +1930,9 @@
   if (info.m_deviceType == AE_DEVTYPE_HDMI)
   {
     int soc_id = aml_get_cpufamily_id();
-    if (soc_id >= AML_S5 || soc_id == AML_T7)
+    // how S5 and later split the formats between hdmi and surround71 is the
+    // AML card's: another card's device takes every format
+    if ((soc_id >= AML_S5 || soc_id == AML_T7) && GetAMLDeviceType(info.m_displayName) != AML_NONE)
     {
       if (device.substr(0, device.find(':')) == "surround71")
       {
